{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"For this sponsor, a **series-trust platform is a sensible starting point—not an automatic winner**.\n\n- **Platform:** Shares an existing trust, board and servicing arrangements, typically reducing launch time and upfront fixed costs. Compare minimum fees, asset-based charges, included services, provider quality, termination costs and portability.\n- **Own trust:** Offers greater influence over governance arrangements, providers, branding and future product development, but requires funding and overseeing legal, board, compliance, administration and other infrastructure. One ETF may struggle to absorb those fixed costs.\n- **Control trade-off:** A platform sponsor generally retains portfolio-management responsibility but accepts shared-board oversight and platform constraints. Its own trust provides more organizational autonomy, not freedom from independent oversight.\n\nModel total costs at realistic asset levels and weigh future launches, specialized needs and operational capacity.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Neither structure guarantees distribution or commercial success; outsourcing infrastructure does not eliminate the sponsor’s responsibilities."}}
